      "content": "To capture demographic volatility, you can model it by tracking the rate of change in key demographic percentages—such as income levels, age distribution, or ethnic makeup—over short timeframes like six to twelve months. The algorithm should assign a higher weighting to areas exhibiting a rapid variance in these stats, indicating an ongoing transition or pressure point. This change rate, rather than the absolute numbers alone, serves as a proxy for underlying social dynamism that correlates with potential friction.",
